<title>GERMANY: TABLE - W.German July adjusted jobless falls 10,000.</title>
<headline>TABLE - W.German July adjusted jobless falls 10,000.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>W.GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT</p>
<p>				 July 97	 June 97	  July 96</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    2.990 million     2.924 million	2.765 million</p>
<p> Number (adj)		3.029 million     3.039 million	2.790 million</p>
<p> Change (adj)		-10,000	 -1,000	   +14,000</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		9.7  pct	 9.5 pct	 9.0 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	91,655	  120,318	  179,490</p>
<p> Vacancies		   295,756	 307,342	  291,681</p>
<p>Change in number in work May 97	  Apr 97</p>
<p>				 -8,000x	 -22,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
